- (709, 0.277) run1: highest modulus but lowest pore fraction among good-quality — non-dominated on modulus axis; but run2 was very different (474, 0.332), indicating poor reproducibility

**Key observation on 17p5-0add-10deg-15s-N2:**
- Run 1: Modulus=709, PF=0.277 (good quality)
- Run 2: Modulus=475, PF=0.332 (wrinkle, 1 specimen fit)
- Run 3: Modulus=516, PF=0.281 (good quality, 1 specimen fit)

Runs 1 and 3 are more consistent with each other (~515–709 range), while run 2 is an outlier with quality issues. The mean of runs 1 and 3 is roughly (612, 0.279). This candidate has the highest modulus among good-quality experiments but pore fraction is on the lower end.

**19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2:** (351, 0.430) — highest pore fraction observed, good quality, but only 1 specimen fit. This is a strong pore-fraction candidate but unvalidated.

