## Step 2: Pareto Front Analysis

Dominance check (maximize both):

- **19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2 run1**: Modulus=350.7, PF=0.4295 — highest pore fraction by far; dominated in modulus but not dominated overall (no point has both higher modulus AND higher PF)
- **18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2**: Modulus=476.8, PF=0.3931 — has top gap defect; but PF is second highest
- **17p5-10deg-15s-N2 run1**: Modulus=708.9, PF=0.2768 — high modulus but lower PF; not dominated (no point beats it on modulus while also having higher PF)
- **17p5-5deg-550s-N2 run1**: Modulus=777.9, PF=0.2730 — highest modulus; has top gap defect
- **17p5-20deg-90s-N2**: Modulus=683.3, PF=0.2824 — good quality, single specimen
- **17p5-25deg-375s-N2**: Modulus=591.7, PF=0.2830 — good quality

Checking for non-dominated points (no other point has both higher modulus AND higher PF):
- 777.9/0.273 — not dominated (highest modulus)
- 708.9/0.277 — not dominated by 777.9 (lower PF); dominated? 777.9 has lower PF, so not dominated
- 683.3/0.282 — 708.9 has higher modulus but lower PF; 777.9 has higher modulus but lower PF → not dominated
- 591.7/0.283 — 683.3 has higher modulus and similar PF (0.282 < 0.283) → 591.7 not dominated by 683.3; 708.9 has higher modulus but lower PF → not dominated
- 547.2/0.311 — 591.7 has higher modulus but lower PF (0.283 < 0.311) → not dominated
- 516.2/0.329 — 547.2 has higher modulus but lower PF → not dominated
- 476.8/0.393 — 516.2 has higher modulus but lower PF → not dominated (top gap defect though)
- 350.7/0.430 — highest PF, not dominated

**Approximate Pareto front** (sorted by modulus descending):
1. 777.9 / 0.273 — top gap defect, single specimen
2. 708.9 / 0.277 — run1 only (run2 gave 474.7/0.332, very different)
3. 683.3 / 0.282 — single specimen, good quality
4. 591.7 / 0.283 — good quality, 2 specimens discarded
5. 547.2 / 0.311 — run2 validated, good quality
6. 516.2 / 0.329 — wrinkle defect
7. 476.8 / 0.393 — top gap defect
8. 350.7 / 0.430 — single specimen, minor wrinkle; run2 had no modulus/PF data

## Step 3: Validation Status Assessment

**Key candidates needing validation:**

- **17p5-10deg-15s-N2 (run1 vs run2)**: Run1: 708.9/0.277; Run2: 474.7/0.332; Run3: 515.7/0.281. These three runs show high variability — modulus ranges 474–709 bar, PF ranges 0.277–0.332. The run1 high modulus is not confirmed. Run3 is closer to run2. This candidate is **not reliably confirmed** at the high-modulus value.

- **17p5-5deg-550s-N2 (run1 vs run2)**: Run1: 777.9/0.273 (top gap defect); Run2: 342.5/0.346 (wrinkle, high CV=0.25). Massive discrepancy — run1 appears to be an outlier or the condition is highly variable. **Not confirmed.**

- **19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2 (run1 vs run2)**: Run1: 350.7/0.430 (good PF); Run2: no modulus/PF data (all fits failed). **Not confirmed for both objectives.**

- **17p5-20deg-90s-N2**: Single specimen with modulus=683.3, PF=0.282, good quality. **Needs validation.**

- **18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2**: 476.8/0.393, top gap defect. Interesting PF but quality concern.

- **17-0add-5deg-run2**: 547.2/0.311, good quality, but this is run2 — run1 doesn't exist in the data with the same parameters (run2 is the only measurement at these exact conditions in the current campaign). Actually checking: condition "17-0add-5deg-cosolv-none-bathSolv-none-0wt-30s-N2-1200s_run2" — this is labeled run2 but there's no run1 with identical parameters in the dataset. So it's a single synthesis.

## Step 4: Priority Decision

The most promising **unvalidated** Pareto-front candidate with good quality and a large apparent gain is **17p5-20deg-90s-N2** (polymer_wt=17.5, mixing_temp=50, bath_temp=20, pullcast_speed=7, nitrogen=True, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=90, nips_bath_wait_time=1250). It showed:
- Modulus = 683.3 bar (high, competitive with run1 of 17p5-10deg)
- PF = 0.2824 (moderate)
- Good membrane quality (no defects)
- Single specimen — needs independent synthesis validation

This is a strong Pareto-front candidate with good quality and no defects, and it has never been independently repeated. Validating it would confirm whether this high-modulus result is reproducible.

The **19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2** condition has the highest pore fraction (0.430) but run2 yielded no modulus/PF data — it needs a repeat that successfully measures both objectives. However, run1 had a single specimen for modulus/PF (SD=0), and run2 completely failed to yield mechanical data. The condition appears unreliable for producing measurable mechanical properties.

**Decision: Validate 17p5-20deg-90s-N2** — it's a clean single-specimen Pareto-front candidate with good quality, high modulus, and no defects. An independent repeat will confirm whether it's genuinely on the Pareto front.

