Non-dominated candidates (no other point beats both objectives simultaneously):
- **350.7 / 0.4295**: highest pore fraction by far
- **476.8 / 0.3931**: second highest pore fraction, but top-gap defect
- **547.2 / 0.3110**: dominates 401.3/0.3159 and 491.1/0.2722
- **591.7 / 0.2830**: dominates 569.3/0.2890 (lower PF), 515.7/0.2813
- **683.3 / 0.2824**: dominates 591.7/0.2830? No — 683.3 has lower PF (0.2824 < 0.2830). Actually 683.3/0.2824 vs 591.7/0.2830: 683.3 wins modulus, 591.7 wins PF → neither dominates
- **708.9 / 0.2768**: dominated by 683.3/0.2824 (lower modulus but higher PF)? 708.9 > 683.3 on modulus, 0.2768 < 0.2824 on PF → neither dominates
- **777.9 / 0.2730**: highest modulus; 0.2730 < 0.2768 → not dominated by 708.9

True Pareto front (quality-filtered, removing severe defects):
- **777.9 / 0.2730** — top-gap defect, unvalidated (run1 only)
- **708.9 / 0.2768** — run1 only, good quality
- **683.3 / 0.2824** — run1 only (1 specimen fit), good quality
- **591.7 / 0.2830** — run1 only, good quality
- **547.2 / 0.3110** — run2 (1 independent run), good quality
- **350.7 / 0.4295** — run1 only, minor wrinkle, 1 specimen fit

The 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s candidate (350.7/0.4295) has a very large apparent pore fraction gain. Run2 of this condition failed to yield modulus/pore fraction measurements (all 4 specimens discarded). So the pore fraction of 0.4295 rests on a single specimen from run1 — this is highly uncertain and unvalidated.

## Step 3: Validation Priority Assessment

Key unvalidated Pareto candidates:
1. **17p5-0add-5deg-550s-N2-1450s** (777.9/0.2730): run1 has top-gap defect; run2 gave very different results (342.5/0.3463, high CV=0.25, wrinkle) — the two runs are highly inconsistent. This candidate is **not reproducible** and should not be prioritized.
2. **17p5-0add-10deg-15s-N2-1800s** (708.9/0.2768 run1): run2 gave 474.7/0.3318 (wrinkle), run3 gave 515.7/0.2813 — three runs show high variability in modulus (709→475→516). Not converging reliably.
3. **17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2-1250s** (683.3/0.2824 run1): run2 had no measurements (all discarded), run3 gave 327.4/0.3196 — very inconsistent. Not reliable.
4. **19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s** (350.7/0.4295 run1): run2 had no measurements. The high pore fraction is unconfirmed.
5. **17p5-0add-25deg-375s-N2-1300s** (591.7/0.2830): only 1 run, good quality membrane.
6. **17-0add-5deg-30s-N2-1200s_run2** (547.2/0.3110): only 1 run, good quality.

The 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s candidate offers the most compelling Pareto improvement if validated — pore fraction of 0.4295 is dramatically higher than anything else, and modulus of 350.7 is lower but the pore fraction gain is enormous. However, run2 yielded zero usable measurements. This is a high-priority validation target.

But wait — run2 of 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s failed completely (all 4 specimens discarded: "insufficient data to fit", "poor plateau fit", "yield point misplaced"). This suggests the condition may be unreliable or the run1 result was a lucky outlier. The run1 result itself was based on only 1 specimen (SD=0 on all mechanical properties). This is very uncertain.

The **17p5-0add-25deg-375s-N2-1300s** (591.7/0.2830) is a solid Pareto candidate with good membrane quality and only 1 run. It offers a good balance of high modulus and moderate pore fraction. Validating this would be informative.

Alternatively, **547.2/0.3110** (17-0add-5deg-30s-N2-1200s_run2) is a confirmed good-quality membrane with decent performance on both objectives, but only 1 run.

Given the instructions to prioritize validation of apparent best/Pareto candidates with large apparent gains or high uncertainty, and that the 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s run1 result (0.4295 pore fraction) is based on a single specimen with run2 completely failing, this is the highest-priority validation. A third independent synthesis attempt would clarify whether this extreme pore fraction is real.

However, I must also consider: run2 of 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s failed completely. The run1 result (350.7 modulus, 0.4295 PF) came from a single specimen. The condition parameters are within bounds. A third run is warranted to determine if this is a real phenomenon.

