## Step 2: Identify Pareto-Non-Dominated Candidates

Sorting by modulus descending and checking pore fraction:

- **17p5-0add-5deg-550s-N2-1450s_run1**: 777.9 bar, 0.273 PF — but top gap defect, single run
- **17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2-1250s_run1**: 683.3 bar, 0.282 PF — single run (run2 missing, run3: 327.4/0.320)
- **17p5-0add-10deg-15s-N2-1800s_run1**: 708.9 bar, 0.277 PF — run2: 474.7/0.332, run3: 515.7/0.281
- **19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s_run1**: 350.7 bar, 0.430 PF — run2 & run3 missing modulus

Pareto front candidates (not dominated on both objectives):
1. **19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s**: highest pore fraction (0.430) but low modulus (350.7) — only 1 run has both measurements; runs 2 & 3 have no modulus
2. **17p5-0add-10deg-15s-N2-1800s**: high modulus (~708.9 run1), moderate PF (0.277) — 3 runs but inconsistent (run2: 474.7, run3: 515.7); run1 had good quality, run2 had wrinkle
3. **17p5-0add-5deg-550s-N2-1450s**: highest modulus (777.9 run1) but top gap defect; run2 was 342.5 with high CV — very inconsistent

## Step 3: Validation Status Assessment

**17p5-0add-10deg-15s-N2-1800s** (polymer_wt=17.5, mixing_temp=65, bath_temp=10, pullcast_speed=6, N2=True, wait=15s, nips=1800s):
- Run1: 708.9 bar / 0.277 PF (good quality)
- Run2: 474.7 bar / 0.332 PF (wrinkle noted, only 1 specimen fit)
- Run3: 515.7 bar / 0.281 PF (good quality, only 1 specimen fit)

Three runs exist but results are inconsistent (708.9 vs 474.7 vs 515.7 bar). The high modulus in run1 is not reproduced. Mean across runs ≈ 566 bar, PF ≈ 0.297. This is a reasonable Pareto candidate but the high-modulus result is not confirmed.

**19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s** (polymer_wt=19.5, mixing_temp=80, bath_temp=25, pullcast_speed=6, N2=False, wait=130s, nips=1550s):
- Run1: 350.7 bar / 0.430 PF (minor wrinkle)
- Run2: no modulus/PF measured
- Run3: no modulus/PF measured

Only 1 run has both objectives measured. This is the highest pore fraction observed (0.430) and is a strong Pareto candidate on the pore-fraction axis. The large apparent gain in pore fraction (0.430 vs ~0.28–0.33 for most others) with only one confirmed measurement warrants validation.

**17p5-0add-5deg-550s-N2-1450s** (run1: 777.9/0.273):
- Run2: 342.5/0.346 — dramatically different, high CV (0.25), wrinkle
- Top gap defect in run1
- Not reliably reproducible; run1 result appears anomalous

## Step 4: Decision

The **19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s** condition is the most compelling unvalidated Pareto candidate:
- Highest pore fraction (0.430) by a large margin — a large apparent gain
- Only 1 run has both objectives measured (runs 2 & 3 failed to yield modulus/PF)
- The pore fraction result needs independent confirmation with a successful full measurement
- Runs 2 & 3 had high discard rates (all 4 specimens failed fit in run2; run3 had 4 failures)
- This condition needs a repeat that successfully yields both modulus and pore fraction measurements

The validation repeat uses the same parameters: mixing_temp=80, bath_temp=25, pullcast_speed=6, nitrogen=False, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=130, nips_bath_wait_time=1550, polymer_wt=19.5, additive_wt=0.

